<ThoughtPost
  title="Most of you will not have most of the things in life (ever)"
  date="2024-06-28"
  description="All of us dream. All of us aspire to be something. But let’s be realistic… the world doesn’t care about you or your dreams."
>

<p>All of us dream. All of us aspire to be something. But let’s be realistic… the world doesn’t care about you or your dreams.</p>

<p>Some of you will never achieve the wealth you want, some of you will never feel the sound of a V12 engine in your sports car, some of you will never smell the fresh paint of a high-rise apartment, some of you will never have a dream job, some of you will never get to work for passion, some of you will never feel flow state, some of you will never step foot on foreign soil just to visit it, and some of you will never see six figures in your account (eight or nine for Indians), and it doesn’t end there...</p>

<p>Some of you will never find true love, some of you will never hear the first cry of your own baby, some of you will never receive a love from your parents again, some of you will never get a pat on the back, some of you will never feel care, some of you will never experience warmth, and some of you will someday lose hope!</p>

<p>Very few work hard enough, are talented enough, have enough support, and are lucky enough to achieve what they want, both in practical and emotional aspects of life. But...</p>

<p>Again, the world doesn’t give a shit. Most of you will never achieve most of the things you want.</p>

<p>So, why are you hoping? Why are you dreaming? Why are you living?</p>

<p>Do you even have a dream? Are you brave enough to live? Or are you a scared little human living on borrowed desires? Are you neglecting the fact that you can’t achieve everything but only a few things? Who are you, do you even ask?</p>

</ThoughtPost>
